	"title"		"TraitPeek - Worker Traits in Building Windows"
	"description"		"[b]See who's good at the job without opening the whisker list.[/b]

TraitPeek shows each worker's traits as small tags right under their portrait in the building window, coloured for that building: Weak Knees is so-so in a Bakery but bad in a mine.

[h2]Features[/h2]
[list]
[*]Trait tags under each worker portrait, matched to the right whisker (also with duplicate names)
[*]Colours per building: green = good here, yellow = so-so, red = bad here, beige = doesn't matter
[*]Fuel-aware: Can't Smell is green and Sickly isn't red where the recipe burns fuel
[*]Your own rules per building or group in a small text file that updates never overwrite
[*]Trait names in the game's language
[*]Hidden while the whisker picker is open; doesn't block clicks
[*]Works in every building with worker slots, also while paused
[*]Event-driven: appears instantly, does nothing while you are not interacting
[/list]

[h2]Your own colours[/h2]
The colours come from built-in rules: [url=https://github.com/ringuh/whiskerwood-traitpeek/blob/main/docs/TraitPeek-defaults.txt]see the default rules on GitHub[/url]. To change them:
[olist]
[*]Open the folder [b]%localappdata%\Whiskerwood\Saved\mods\[/b] (paste it into the Explorer address bar).
[*]Create a folder [b]TraitPeekConfig[/b] there.
[*]In it, create a text file named [b]TraitPeek.txt[/b] (it must end in .txt; check that Windows didn't make it TraitPeek.txt.txt).
[*]Write your rules in it, save, and load your save game.
[/olist]
Your file only adds to the defaults: lines apply top to bottom and the last matching line wins, so you only write what you want to change. Mod updates never touch this folder.
[code]
; Bakery: Swift good, Rebellious doesn't matter
[bakery]
green = swift
neutral = rebellious

; your own group of buildings
[groups]
kitchens = Bakery, stewery, fineKitchen

[kitchens]
red = sickly
[/code]
[list]
[*][b]Sections:[/b] all, fuel, nofuel, a group name (factory, extraction, service, school, research, fishing, docks or your own) or a building id
[*][b]Keys:[/b] green, yellow, red, neutral (neutral removes the colour)
[*][b]Values:[/b] trait ids, comma-separated
[/list]
Building ids, trait ids and the full format: [url=https://github.com/ringuh/whiskerwood-traitpeek#configuration]Configuration on GitHub[/url].

[h2]Source[/h2]
[url=https://github.com/ringuh/whiskerwood-traitpeek]GitHub[/url]

Created using the [url=https://github.com/Whiskerwood-Modding/Whiskerwood-Project]Whiskerwood modkit[/url]."
	"changenote"		"1.2: Your own colour rules now load. The file is Saved\mods\TraitPeekConfig\TraitPeek.txt (the game only reads .txt files, so TraitPeek.ini from 1.1 was ignored); rename it if you made one."
